Remove dead entries from the three-dot app menu: the "Passwords and autofill"
submenu, "Send to your devices", and "Translate...".

The earlier settings patch only removed the Autofill entry from the
chrome://settings left-hand navigation. The same surfaces are still reachable
from the app menu, which carries its own "Passwords and autofill" submenu:
Google Password Manager, Payment methods, Contact info (or "Addresses and
more" when the YourSavedInfoSettingsPage feature is off), Identity documents
and Travel. All of those are Google-account-backed services Aerium does not
talk to, so the whole submenu goes rather than individual rows - dropping the
rows alone would leave an empty submenu behind.

The submenu model class is deleted along with its only instantiation so it
does not linger as unreferenced code in the anonymous namespace. The element
identifiers it used (kPasswordManagerMenuItem and friends) are intentionally
left declared and defined, because other translation units still reference
them.

"Send to your devices" is removed from the Save-and-share submenu here, and
neutered at its source in the companion hunk below so no other entry point
(page/link context menu, omnibox sharing icon, sharing hub) resurrects it.

"Translate..." is removed for the same reason, and is handled here rather
than in aerium-remove-translate-settings.patch so that app_menu_model.cc
stays under exactly one patch - a second patch editing this file would have
to be diffed against the post-this-patch state and would accumulate its own
independent offsets, which is how the two would eventually collide.
aerium-remove-translate-settings.patch removed the translate section from
chrome://settings and ungoogled-chromium neuters the translate backend, but
the app-menu row survived both and rendered as a permanently greyed-out item:
IDC_SHOW_TRANSLATE is only ever enabled when the command controller finds a
translatable page, which never happens once the backend is gone. Removing the
row removes the dead UI rather than leaving an entry that can never be
clicked.

The IDC_SHOW_TRANSLATE case in AppMenuModel::LogMenuMetrics goes with it,
because it becomes unreachable: LogMenuMetrics is called from
AppMenuModel::ExecuteCommand for items in this model, and the only other
caller is the callback handed to RecentTabsSubMenuModel, which only ever
forwards recent-tab commands. MENU_ACTION_SHOW_TRANSLATE itself is left
defined - it is a logged histogram enum value, and those are never renumbered
or removed.

# Rebased onto Chromium 152. Two things moved. send_tab_to_self's
# GetEntryPointDisplayReason() gained a second parameter, so the stub takes it
# too. And the app menu's Send-to-your-devices item is now built by
# SaveAndShareSubMenuModel through one of two helpers - a device submenu when
# the feature is offered, a plain item otherwise - so the plain one is what
# gets emptied: the submenu branch needs kOfferFeature, which the stub above
# can no longer return, and emptying a helper that takes no parameters leaves
# nothing unused behind.

--- a/chrome/browser/send_tab_to_self/send_tab_to_self_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/send_tab_to_self/send_tab_to_self_util.cc
@@ -70,18 +70,15 @@ PageContext::FormFieldInfo ExtractFormFieldsFromWebContentsInternal(
 }  // namespace
 
 std::optional<EntryPointDisplayReason> GetEntryPointDisplayReason(
-    content::WebContents* web_contents,
-    const std::optional<GURL>& url) {
-  if (!web_contents) {
-    return std::nullopt;
-  }
-
-  send_tab_to_self::SendTabToSelfSyncService* service =
-      SendTabToSelfSyncServiceFactory::GetForProfile(
-          Profile::FromBrowserContext(web_contents->GetBrowserContext()));
-  const GURL& url_to_check = url.value_or(web_contents->GetLastCommittedURL());
-  return service ? service->GetEntryPointDisplayReason(url_to_check)
-                 : std::nullopt;
+    content::WebContents* /*web_contents*/,
+    const std::optional<GURL>& /*url*/) {
+  // Aerium: "Send to your devices" is a Google-account sync feature. Returning
+  // no display reason removes every entry point at once - the page and link
+  // context menus, the omnibox sharing icon and the sharing hub - instead of
+  // leaving any of them behind as a dead or greyed-out item. The app menu is
+  // handled separately in app_menu_model.cc, which adds its item without
+  // consulting this.
+  return std::nullopt;
 }
 
 bool ShouldDisplayEntryPoint(content::WebContents* web_contents,
